  One of the first printed works in Polish was prepared by the German printer
  Johann Haller, active in Kraków, who followed the German custom of
  using the sequence \textit{rv} (with a round \textit{r}) for the
  letter \textit{w}.

  There also existed a distinct letter \textit{w}, resembling the
  ligature \textit{rv} but with a straight \textit{r}. The Hieronimus
  font created by Anna Wieluńska covers many characters used in old
  Polish publications, including this very character.
